{"id":"CVE-2017-3204","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"certcc","published":"2017-04-04T14:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-08-05T14:16:28.305Z","description":"The Go SSH library (x/crypto/ssh) by default does not verify host keys, facilitating man-in-the-middle attacks. Default behavior changed in commit e4e2799 to require explicitly registering a hostkey verification mechanism.","cwe":["CWE-310 CWE-310"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"Go","product":"SSH library","versions":["affected prior to commit e4e2799"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://godoc.org/golang.org/x/crypto/ssh","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"https://github.com/golang/go/issues/19767","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"https://bridge.grumpy-troll.org/2017/04/golang-ssh-security/","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"https://github.com/golang/crypto/commit/e4e2799dd7aab89f583e1d898300d96367750991","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"http://www.securityfocus.com/bid/97481","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_BID"],"name":"97481"}],"vendors":["golang"]}
{"id":"CVE-2017-8932","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"mitre","published":"2017-07-06T16:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-08-05T16:48:22.902Z","description":"A bug in the standard library ScalarMult implementation of curve P-256 for amd64 architectures in Go before 1.7.6 and 1.8.x before 1.8.2 causes incorrect results to be generated for specific input points. An adaptive attack can be mounted to progressively extract the scalar input to ScalarMult by submitting crafted points and observing failures to the derive correct output. This leads to a full key recovery attack against static ECDH, as used in popular JWT libraries.","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://groups.google.com/d/msg/golang-announce/B5ww0iFt1_Q/TgUFJV14BgAJ","tags":["mailing-list","x_refsource_MLIST"],"name":"[golang-announce] 20170523  [security] Go 1.7.6 and Go 1.8.2 are released"},{"url":"https://github.com/golang/go/commit/9294fa2749ffee7edbbb817a0ef9fe633136fa9c","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2017:1859","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_REDHAT"],"name":"RHSA-2017:1859"},{"url":"http://lists.opensuse.org/opensuse-updates/2017-06/msg00080.html","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_SUSE"],"name":"openSUSE-SU-2017:1650"},{"url":"http://lists.opensuse.org/opensuse-updates/2017-06/msg00079.html","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_SUSE"],"name":"openSUSE-SU-2017:1649"},{"url":"https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=1455191","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"https://github.com/golang/go/issues/20040","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"https://go-review.googlesource.com/c/41070/","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"https://lists.fedoraproject.org/archives/list/package-announce%40lists.fedoraproject.org/message/LZH4T47ROLZ6YEZBDVXVS2KISTDMXAPS/","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_FEDORA"],"name":"FEDORA-2017-278f46fcd6"}],"vendors":["golang"]}
{"id":"CVE-2017-15041","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"mitre","published":"2017-10-05T21:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-08-05T19:42:22.368Z","description":"Go before 1.8.4 and 1.9.x before 1.9.1 allows \"go get\" remote command execution. Using custom domains, it is possible to arrange things so that example.com/pkg1 points to a Subversion repository but example.com/pkg1/pkg2 points to a Git repository. If the Subversion repository includes a Git checkout in its pkg2 directory and some other work is done to ensure the proper ordering of operations, \"go get\" can be tricked into reusing this Git checkout for the fetch of code from pkg2. If the Subversion repository's Git checkout has malicious commands in .git/hooks/, they will execute on the system running \"go get.\"","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2017:3463","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_REDHAT"],"name":"RHSA-2017:3463"},{"url":"https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2018:0878","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_REDHAT"],"name":"RHSA-2018:0878"},{"url":"https://golang.org/cl/68190","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"http://www.securityfocus.com/bid/101196","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_BID"],"name":"101196"},{"url":"https://golang.org/cl/68022","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"https://security.gentoo.org/glsa/201710-23","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_GENTOO"],"name":"GLSA-201710-23"},{"url":"https://groups.google.com/d/msg/golang-dev/RinSE3EiJBI/kYL7zb07AgAJ","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"https://github.com/golang/go/issues/22125","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"https://lists.debian.org/debian-lts-announce/2021/03/msg00014.html","tags":["mailing-list","x_refsource_MLIST"],"name":"[debian-lts-announce] 20210313 [SECURITY] [DLA 2591-1] golang-1.7 security update"},{"url":"https://lists.debian.org/debian-lts-announce/2021/03/msg00015.html","tags":["mailing-list","x_refsource_MLIST"],"name":"[debian-lts-announce] 20210313 [SECURITY] [DLA 2592-1] golang-1.8 security update"}],"vendors":["golang"]}
{"id":"CVE-2017-15042","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"mitre","published":"2017-10-05T21:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-08-05T19:42:22.302Z","description":"An unintended cleartext issue exists in Go before 1.8.4 and 1.9.x before 1.9.1. RFC 4954 requires that, during SMTP, the PLAIN auth scheme must only be used on network connections secured with TLS. The original implementation of smtp.PlainAuth in Go 1.0 enforced this requirement, and it was documented to do so. In 2013, upstream issue #5184, this was changed so that the server may decide whether PLAIN is acceptable. The result is that if you set up a man-in-the-middle SMTP server that doesn't advertise STARTTLS and does advertise that PLAIN auth is OK, the smtp.PlainAuth implementation sends the username and password.","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2017:3463","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_REDHAT"],"name":"RHSA-2017:3463"},{"url":"https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2018:0878","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_REDHAT"],"name":"RHSA-2018:0878"},{"url":"http://www.securityfocus.com/bid/101197","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_BID"],"name":"101197"},{"url":"https://golang.org/cl/68210","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"https://golang.org/cl/68023","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"https://github.com/golang/go/issues/22134","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"https://security.gentoo.org/glsa/201710-23","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_GENTOO"],"name":"GLSA-201710-23"},{"url":"https://groups.google.com/d/msg/golang-dev/RinSE3EiJBI/kYL7zb07AgAJ","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]}],"vendors":["golang"]}
{"id":"CVE-2017-20146","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"Go","published":"2022-12-27T21:13:00.461Z","updated":"2025-04-11T23:02:21.962Z","title":"Improper access control in github.com/gorilla/handlers","description":"Usage of the CORS handler may apply improper CORS headers, allowing the requester to explicitly control the value of the Access-Control-Allow-Origin header, which bypasses the expected behavior of the Same Origin Policy.","cwe":["CWE 284: Improper Access Control"],"metrics":[{"src":"CISA-ADP","v":"3.1","score":9.8,"sev":"CRITICAL","vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H"},{"src":"CISA-ADP","ssvc":{"Exploitation":"none","Automatable":"yes","Technical Impact":"total"}}],"affected":[{"vendor":"github.com/gorilla/handlers","product":"github.com/gorilla/handlers","packageName":"github.com/gorilla/handlers","collectionURL":"https://pkg.go.dev","defaultStatus":"unaffected","versions":["affected 0 <1.3.0 (semver)"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://github.com/gorilla/handlers/pull/116"},{"url":"https://github.com/gorilla/handlers/commit/90663712d74cb411cbef281bc1e08c19d1a76145"},{"url":"https://pkg.go.dev/vuln/GO-2020-0020"}],"credits":["Evan J Johnson"],"vendors":["golang"]}
